6. Arrays - Variables that store multiple values

    An array stores multiple elements of the same types.

        int numbers[5] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

    Access each element using an index starting at zero.

        printf("%d\n", numbers[0]); // 10
        printf("%d\n", numbers[2]); // 30

    Character arrays can store strings.

        char    name[];

        name = 'Alex';

    This array contains the characters A,l,e,x and the null terminator '\0'.
